in/2ccd9fef.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/2ccd9fef.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPredict the next panel in a framed sequence by continuing each scheduled colored interval.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid is made from three or more equal panels in one row or one column.\n- The final input panel is the static target template; every earlier panel differs from it only by dynamic colors absent from the template.\n- Each dynamic color appears in a regular temporal schedule across the earlier panels.\n\nRule\n- Keep the final template panel as the output canvas.\n- For every dynamic color whose schedule reaches the next panel, compare its last two appearances.\n- Extrapolate each one-dimensional interval along the color's changing row or column axis and paint that predicted mask.\n\nKey insight\n- The task is not asking for the last visible panel, but for the next frame after the blank/template slot.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"sequence of equal rectangular panels ending with a blank/static template panel\",\n  \"dst\": \"next panel in the sequence\",\n  \"transform\": \"use the template panel as the output canvas; for each dynamic color absent from the template, follow its regular panel schedule and extrapolate the last two interval changes one more step along the changing row or column axis\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"same shape as one panel\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2c181942\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3194\nmechanism=0.3757\nlexical=0.0195\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:axis, object:frame, operation:reflect, operation:rotate, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/2c181942.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/2c181942.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nAttach monochrome sprites to the matching sides of a central hollow square.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. A hollow NxN square (hub) with bg corners/interior and four differently-colored edges (top, bottom, left, right).\n- 2-4 monochrome sprites scattered on the grid, each matching one hub edge color.\n\nRule:\n- For each hub edge color, find the matching sprite outside the hub.\n- Rotate the sprite (0/90/180/270°) so its contact edge has exactly N-2 contiguous cells aligned with the hub side, and the rotated sprite is mirror-symmetric along the contact-edge axis (UD for left/right, LR for top/bottom).\n- Translate it to adjoin that hub side. \n- Clear everything else to bg; output is hub + attached sprites only.\n\nKey insight: Each edge color uniquely pairs a sprite to a side; symmetry along the contact-edge axis disambiguates the correct rotation.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"solid monochrome sprite s\",\n  \"dst\": \"attach to an edge of hollow polychrome sprite d with bg corners and 4 differently-colored side edges\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.head.color == d.edge.color and s.head.length == d.edge.length\",\n  \"transform\": \"rotate s to align matching edge with d.side\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"135a2760\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3296\nmechanism=0.4517\nlexical=0.0122\ncode_feature=0.1667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:axis, object:frame, object:rectangle, operation:reflect, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/135a2760.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/135a2760.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRepair noisy periodic patterns inside frame-delimited grid regions.\n\nInput structure:\n- Frame color (most common) forms full rows/cols, dividing the grid into rectangular regions.\n- bg (second most common) fills empty space; each region contains a small colored tile repeated periodically with a few corrupted pixels