ks of two periodic\nframe patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the\nmissing two anchor copies.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"two same-color solid rectangular anchors, with two right control bars and two below control bars beside the upper-left anchor\",\n  \"dst\": \"the missing two anchor corners and periodic frame segments between all four anchors\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy the anchor rectangle into the missing corners; repeat the right-control colors across the top and bottom anchor rows and outer borders, and repeat the below-control colors down the left and right side bars using the same spacing\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6165ea8f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3093\nmechanism=0.3626\nlexical=0.0139\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:axis, object:template, operation:reflect, operation:rotate, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6165ea8f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/6165ea8f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nBuild a color-labeled shape-equivalence table from the objects listed on the right edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background contains one main 4-connected object for each foreground color.\n- The rightmost column has one singleton pixel of each foreground color, listed top-to-bottom.\n- Those singleton pixels define the row and column order of the output table.\n\nRule:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
